  {
   "id": "oq01Qd1-BgAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2019-06-06T11:29:05Z",
   "subject": "Re: Question about HTMT (semTools)",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><p>I think that Henesler et. al. proposed to use the geometric for the latter. Therefore I am not Sure what has been implemented in semTools?</p></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I didn&#39;t write this function myself, but it&#39;s not long if you want to check out the source code.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/simsem/semTools/blob/master/semTools/R/htmt.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/simsem/semTools/blob/master/semTools/R/htmt.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423568242000&amp;usg=AOvVaw249niq0Rzr_7Fu04WET_Mv\">https://github.com/simsem/semTools/blob/master/semTools/R/htmt.R</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Looks like the arithmetic mean is provided using the mean() function.  If you can provide the full reference for the article that advocates (and makes a strong case) for the geometric mean instead, I can easily add that as an optional argument.</div><div><br></div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423568242000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1eHY8O6qu__23q1VohQKae\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "qUNRSRCiAQAJ",
   "from": "Ibrahim Nasser",
