   "subject": "Re: Question about HTMT (semTools)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">\r\nHi,\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>The htmt code does geometric mean, but the documentation appears incorrect. Here is the code for geometric mean.</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<table style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-collapse:collapse;border-spacing:0px;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">\r\n<tbody style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">\r\n<tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">\r\n<td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px 10px;line-height:20px;vertical-align:top;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow:visible;white-space:pre;word-wrap:normal\">\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">for</span> (<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">i</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">in</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,92,197)\">1</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">:</span>nrow(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">comb</span>)) {</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">\r\n<td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px 10px;color:rgba(27,31,35,0.298039);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:20px;min-width:50px;text-align:right;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap;width:50px\">\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px 10px;line-height:20px;vertical-align:top;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow:visible;white-space:pre;word-wrap:normal\">\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">g</span>[[<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">i</span>]]\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&lt;-</span> sqrt(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">m.cor.w</span>[<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">comb</span>[<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">i</span>,\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,92,197)\">2</span>]]\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">*</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">m.cor.w</span>[<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">comb</span>[<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">i</span>,\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,92,197)\">1</span>]])</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">\r\n<td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px 10px;color:rgba(27,31,35,0.298039);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:20px;min-width:50px;text-align:right;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap;width:50px\">\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px 10px;line-height:20px;vertical-align:top;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow:visible;white-space:pre;word-wrap:normal\">\r\n}</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Mikko</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n<div><br>\r\n<blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n<div>On 6 Jun 2019, at 13.29, Terrence Jorgensen &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tjorge...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div>\r\n<br>\r\n</blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<p>I think that Henesler et. al. proposed to use the geometric for the latter. Therefore I am not Sure what has been implemented in semTools?</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>I didn&#39;t write this function myself, but it&#39;s not long if you want to check out the source code.</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><a href=\"https://github.com/simsem/semTools/blob/master/semTools/R/htmt.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/simsem/semTools/blob/master/semTools/R/htmt.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423568245000&amp;usg=AOvVaw01wZWohkb1Mk5DEl5nZJaS\">https://github.com/simsem/semTools/blob/master/semTools/R/htmt.R</a><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Looks like the arithmetic mean is provided using the mean() function.  If you can provide the full reference for the article that advocates (and makes a strong case) for the geometric mean instead, I can easily add that as an optional argument.</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div>\r\n<div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div>\r\n<div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div>\r\n<div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423568246000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ji6A-kxxZyxF7F7vydi68\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
