  {
   "id": "wkm72YiABgAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2019-06-06T11:59:42Z",
   "subject": "Re: Question about HTMT (semTools)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div>The htmt code does geometric mean... Here is the code for geometric mean.<br></div></div></blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;border-spacing:0px;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0px 10px;line-height:20px;vertical-align:top;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow:visible;white-space:pre;word-wrap:normal\">\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(215,58,73)\">for</span> (<span>i</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(215,58,73)\">in</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(215,58,73)\">:</span>nrow(<span>comb</span>)) {</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0px 10px;color:rgba(27,31,35,0.298039);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:20px;min-width:50px;text-align:right;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap;width:50px\">\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0px 10px;line-height:20px;vertical-align:top;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow:visible;white-space:pre;word-wrap:normal\">\r\n<span>g</span>[[<span>i</span>]]\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&lt;-</span> sqrt(<span>m.cor.w</span>[<span>comb</span>[<span>i</span>,\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197)\">2</span>]]\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(215,58,73)\">*</span>\r\n<span>m.cor.w</span>[<span>comb</span>[<span>i</span>,\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197)\">1</span>]])</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0px 10px;color:rgba(27,31,35,0.298039);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:20px;min-width:50px;text-align:right;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap;width:50px\">\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0px 10px;line-height:20px;vertical-align:top;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow:visible;white-space:pre;word-wrap:normal\">\r\n}</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Ah right, thanks Mikko!  </div><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">but the documentation appears incorrect</blockquote><div> </div><div>What part?  Should I change the description to read &quot;geometric-mean correlation&quot; instead of the vague &quot;average correlation&quot;?</div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">The full text of the article is available here (open access): <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Flink.springer.com%2Farticle%2F10.1007%2Fs11747-014-0403-8&amp;sa=D&amp;sntz=1&amp;usg=AFQjCNHlF1nawSDmeUVVmvtgtgc_EoPxKw\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.google.com/url?q%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Flink.springer.com%252Farticle%252F10.1007%252Fs11747-014-0403-8%26sa%3DD%26sntz%3D1%26usg%3DAFQjCNHlF1nawSDmeUVVmvtgtgc_EoPxKw&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423568247000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0IVAz3pDcpXTPrMGS6vroi\">https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11747-014-0403-8</a></blockquote><div><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div>OK, that&#39;s the one already in the References on the help page.  Thanks!</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><br></div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423568247000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0gkvTgR7zLiD6ROPh52Mk7\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
